# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Rift — environment
#
# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env.local is gitignored and must stay that
# way; nothing in this file should ever hold a real value.
#
# Every service below is documented in docs/integrations.md — what it is for,
# what it costs, what happens when it is missing, and which build phase wires
# it. The prototype at /prototype needs NONE of these: it runs with an empty
# env file, which is the point of it.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── Supabase ─────────────────────────────────────────── auth, database, files
# Project → Settings → API. The anon key is public by design; RLS is what
# protects the data, so never ship a table without a policy.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# Server-only. Bypasses RLS entirely — never expose it to the browser and never
# prefix it with NEXT_PUBLIC_. Needed for migrations, seeding, and jobs.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Set to `local` to run auth against localStorage with no Supabase project at
# all. Useful offline; remove it for anything real.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_AUTH_MODE=local


# ── Sentry ────────────────────────────────────────── errors and performance
# Failures must surface, never fail silently (docs/handoff.md §5 rule 4).
NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=
# Optional server/edge override; falls back to NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN.
# SENTRY_DSN=

# Source-map upload on `next build`. Set in CI and on Vercel, not locally —
# without a token, `next.config.ts` disables sourcemap upload rather than failing.
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=
# SENTRY_ORG=
# SENTRY_PROJECT=


# ── Brevo ──────────────────────────────────── transactional email + contacts
# Missing key = every send no-ops cleanly and reports `skipped`. That is the
# correct dev behaviour and it is deliberate: see lib/brevo/sync.ts.
# If the API returns 401 "unrecognised IP", whitelist at Security → Authorised IPs.
# BREVO_API_KEY=
#
# The sending address, which Brevo must have verified. Without it every send is
# rejected at the API, so it is treated as missing configuration rather than
# defaulted — an unconfigured deployment reports "not configured" instead of
# failing every message with a confusing 400.
# BREVO_FROM_EMAIL=
#
# One-time attribute bootstrap, after setting the key:
#   npm run brevo:ensure-attributes


# ── Scheduler ────────────────────────────────────────── the nurture cadence
# Shared secret for /api/nurture/run. Without it the endpoint refuses to run at
# all — an unauthenticated endpoint that sends email on demand is a way to have
# your sending reputation destroyed by a stranger with curl.
# CRON_SECRET=


# ── Calendar ───────────────────────────────────────── consultation booking
# Phase 3. /prototype/book currently fakes the confirmation; speed-to-lead is
# only real once a stranger can take a slot without a human in the path.
# CAL_API_KEY=
# CAL_EVENT_TYPE_ID=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CAL_LINK=


# ── Not yet chosen ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Both are needed by features already specified in the prototype. Until they
# exist, the code paths must degrade honestly rather than pretend — see
# docs/integrations.md for exactly how.
#
# SMS. Without it, every text step in the nurture cadence permanently
# downgrades to email (lib/prototype/nurture.ts, resolveChannel). The TCPA
# consent gate is already built and is what makes texting lawful at all.
# TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=
# TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=
# TWILIO_MESSAGING_SERVICE_SID=
#
# E-signature. Representation agreements gate the client journey and block
# plan publishing (lib/prototype/seam.ts, canPublish). Today `rep` is a status
# field with nothing behind it.
# ESIGN_API_KEY=
